From dfc95048fd450c92847f319ef904fde8bb478488 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <mia.ailab1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:09:36 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] MiniMax-M3.1-Flash: interface, weights and native
 registration (T9, host half)

Adds the minimax_m3 engine contract (iface.zig: Part/Resume/Marks/Cancel/Seg, the follower
header, window widths, the conformsEngine/conformsNative checks) and resolves the 13
GLM-reuse mismatches M1-M13 (docs/interface-decisions.md); per-rank weight descriptors from
load.Plan and the experts' pointer/width tables (weights.zig), a device loader with direct
I/O, a page-cache drop after each shard and a header-only checkpoint digest
(weights_device.zig); the host half of the page state (pages.zig); native.zig for model_type
minimax_m3_vl (format exl3) registered in the CUDA registry, whose open() checks the ranks,
settings, plan and budget and then stops with error.EngineNotBuilt (no forward pass yet).

Host patches: kv_pool.Layout.all_paged and Plan.paged (every stream pages), a
backend-owned radix prompt cache (owns_prompt_cache, cache_limit, Info.prompt_cache), the
MiniMax think markers chosen by tokenizer and the prompt's tail, thinking_mode written as
enabled/disabled for MiniMax's template, a MiniMax tool-grammar style that refuses required
tool_choice, TF_ROCE/TF_ROCE_MAX_KB in the rank fingerprint, and one host memory budget
(Options.grant, budget.hosted). Every other family's behaviour is unchanged.

No GPU was available: host tests and compile checks only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
